variables = a word that acctually stores a value like some string int 
types
1.var = from ES5 function scoped could be declared twice with the different value
2.let = from ES6 blocked scoped and the value could be changed
3.const = also from the ES6 but the scope is global and value cannot be changed 

temporal dead zone = when we execute the variable before its initialization
hoisting = when a variable is made its declaration goes on top of the code but the initialization remains in its place so that makes the temporal dead zone and it happens in all three types of variables var,let,const but the var shows "UNDEFINED" and let, const gives a refrence error



starting:-

so the javascript cant be executed without having any html file so to make the java script work in our browser we must create the html file and then add the js file in the body.

DataTypes:-
primitive = with the brackets eg:- [arrays] {objects} (functions)
refrences = without any brackets:- strings,number,booleans etc.


integer = number
string = set of characters 
null = value is empty
undefined = a value that is not defined yet by default its undefined given by the java script engine
symbol = an unique value that cannot be changed 
bigint = allows us to use more value than the java script acctually supports by default


Dynamic typing = js changes and chooses the data type of the value on the basis of the value assigned to the variable and later if the value changes the data type also changes we don not need to define that some variable is an integer or a boolean java script shall do that on its own and this functionality is called dynamic typing.


quirks:-
"typeof" = to know the type of the value (u could check this in the console windows of the broweser)
"NaN" = not a number (an operation that cannot be performed but it is realated to number its a failed number operation word)



type coercion:-

when the java scripts changes the data types of the value automatically 
example:- 


let a = "5" + 1

output = 51

the js engine changed the data type of the 1 and converted it into the string to concatt the values so the operation could be performed 

let "5" - 1

output = 4

js changed the data type of 5 into an integer and performed the equation (in js + is used for the two tasks first is for adding the value and the other one is to concatinate two values so whhenever there is a string and a integer the string would always gets its data type changed )


truthy and falsy values :-

falsy values = 0 , null , undefined , NaN , document.all
truthy = remaining all are truthy



operators in js :- are used to perform an operation in js it could be an mathmatical operation or a logical


arithmetic: + - * % / **
 + is used to used to add the values of two numbers but it also used to concatinate (har+sh = harsh) the strings or the output 
 - substract
 / divide
 * multiplication
 % reminder/percentage but in js it is called "mod"
 ** expontiation used to do  2 power of 3 = 8 such operations 



comparison: == === != !== <= >=' < >
 == used to check that if the two values are same or not but it only checks the value not the data types of the values 
 === same as double equal but also checks the data type of the value makes comparison more stricker
 != not equal 
 !== same as not equal operator but more sticker than that (also checks the data type)
 > greater than 
 < less than 
 >= greater equal just as the greater than operator same with the =<

logical:
&&: works as the AND gate TT if the both values are true then the output should be true 
|| or operator if one is true the output is true 
! not operator makes the output opposite of its true output if the ans is true and if we use not operator then the output shall be false 


